From 5ec6977c8d3ad279fce465b6f11bdf11897694bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:08:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6150-samsung-a70q: correct Venus
 OPPs

The downstream Galaxy A70 device tree exposes video clock rates only
up to 410 MHz. The inherited 460 MHz OPP has no matching firmware level.

Remove it so Linux cannot request an unsupported performance level.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
index ebdba14c4..7a53334d6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
@@ -273,6 +273,11 @@ opp-745000000 {
 	};
 };
 
+/* The A70 firmware does not expose the 460 MHz video clock level. */
+&venus_opp_table {
+	/delete-node/ opp-460000000;
+};
+
 /*
  * The Samsung firmware requires platform-specific preparation before CPU
  * power collapse.  Keep the architectural WFI idle state until that support
